# README sync (Alfred Identity Backend)

When you change user-visible behavior, API routes, env vars, Discord commands, web admin tabs, or project layout, update **README.md** in the same change (or immediately after).

## What to keep in sync

- **Help section** — Compose quick start, SSO token flow, access model, Discord commands, web admin tabs
- **Endpoints table** — `/health`, `/ws/sso`, `/admin/` (do not document routes that are not implemented)
- **Project layout** — `cmd/` and `internal/` packages
- **Environment variables** — must match `.env.example` and `internal/config/config.go`
- **Discord commands** — must match `internal/discord/bot.go` (`commandDefs`, subcommands)
- **Web admin tabs** — must match `TABS` in `internal/web/static/app.js`
- **Branding** — `Alfred Identity Management` (web), `Alfred Identity` (desktop GUI); see `internal/web/names.go`

## Sources of truth

| Topic | Check |
|-------|--------|
| Env vars | `.env.example`, `internal/config/config.go` |
| Discord slash commands | `internal/discord/bot.go` |
| Web admin UI | `internal/web/static/app.js`, `internal/web/names.go` |
| HTTP routes | `cmd/daemon/main.go`, `internal/web/server.go` |
| SSO source JSON shape | `internal/web/source_import.go`, Discord `handleSSO` |
| Tests / coverage | `Makefile`, `scripts/test.sh`, `.github/workflows/test.yml` |

## Do not

- Document `/sso create` — the subcommand is **`get`** (creates if missing)
- Document `GET /sso-source.json` unless a handler exists in `internal/web/server.go` or `cmd/daemon/main.go`
- Describe GUI flows that belong in the `alfred-identity` README — link there instead

Keep README concise; link to `docs/` for long setup guides.
